course: dictionary
lesson: 10131
title: A threat is a warning of harm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A threat is a warning that something bad will happen, or a sign that danger is coming. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning fits. «Threats are a reason to stop and tell, not to keep talking.» Here a threat is something serious, because the sentence tells you to stop and tell someone.
explain: Sometimes a threat is something that could cause harm, like a storm or a disease. «Sea urchins are covered with movable spines that point towards a threat.» The spines point towards danger, so a threat is something that could hurt them.
explain: A threat can also be a sign that something bad may happen. «A threat of rain» means the sky looks like rain may come soon. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: When someone makes a threat to hurt you, or tries to make you do something by scaring you, tell a trusted adult the same day. Never keep a threat secret.
fact: A threat is a noun: a threat, threats.
fact: «Threat» means a promise to hurt someone, or something that could cause danger or harm.
fact: «A threat of rain» means a sign that rain may come.
fact: Useful phrases: «make a threat», «under threat», «a threat to», «an empty threat».
fact: Threats to animals include pollution and habitat loss, which means losing the places where they live.
exercise: «Threats are a reason to stop and tell, not to keep talking.» What should you do when you meet a threat? | Ignore it and say nothing | Reply to it with a threat of your own | Keep it secret | *Tell a trusted adult
exercise: «Sea urchins are covered with movable spines that point towards a threat.» What does threat mean here? | A kind of seaweed | *Something that could cause harm | The sea urchin's mouth | A friendly visitor
exercise: «There is a threat of rain this afternoon.» What does threat of rain mean? | A dry, sunny afternoon | Rain has already stopped | A rainbow in the sky | *A sign that rain may come
test: The wild birds are ___ because their forest is being cut down. | *under threat | an empty threat | a threat of | threat to sleep
test: «He said he would tell everyone a secret, but it was an empty threat.» What does empty threat mean? | A threat that is very loud | A promise to be kind | A threat written on paper | *A threat that will not really happen
exam: Someone you do not know sends you the message «meet me at the gate». What should you do? | Keep it secret | Delete it and forget about it | Reply and go to the gate | *Tell a teacher or parent the same day
